<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer unit plans to cut 120 jobs.</title>
<headline>Sulzer unit plans to cut 120 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A drop in orders at Sulzer AG unit SLM Schweizerische Lokomotiv- und Maschinenfabrik AG has led to plans for a cut in the workforce by up to 120 jobs in 1997, Sulzer said.</p>
<p>&quot;The foreseen lack of orders force the concern to reduce its capacity by 120 positions,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>It said that its business with locomotive engines has been faced with &quot;large fluctuations in demand.&quot; After large orders in the early 1990s, in the last three years there had been a drop in orders.</p>
<p>A company official said that the unit currently employs slightly more than 700 people.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
